<title>POLAND: POLISH NEW CAR SALES UP 30 PCT IN APRIL.</title>
<headline>POLISH NEW CAR SALES UP 30 PCT IN APRIL.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>New car sales in Poland grew by 29.9 percent in January-April against the same period last year to 174,224 units, an independent car market monitoring agency, Samar, said in a report on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Samar said sales of commercial vehicles rose 32.2 percent to 17,886 over the same period.</p>
<p>Fiat topped the list of passenger car makers with 60,742 units sold and a 34.9 percent market share.</p>
